From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Druchenko <bananos@dev.co.ua>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:25:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] b43: accept radio 2057 rev 13 on N-PHY (experimental)

The BCM5357/53572 SoCs (e.g. ASUS RT-N12 D1) have an N-PHY rev 17 with
radio 2057 rev 13. b43 rejects that radio at probe. Accept it with a
warning, so the probe, board data, firmware and PHY init can be tested;
the radio still has no init or channel tables.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
index 7d73480..7d28a5c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -4636,8 +4636,11 @@ static int b43_phy_versioning(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 		    radio_id != 0x2057)
 			unsupported = 1;
 		if (radio_id == 0x2057 &&
-		    !(radio_rev == 9 || radio_rev == 14))
+		    !(radio_rev == 9 || radio_rev == 13 || radio_rev == 14))
 			unsupported = 1;
+		if (radio_id == 0x2057 && radio_rev == 13)
+			b43warn(dev->wl, "Radio 2057 rev 13 (BCM5357/53572) has no "
+				"init or channel tables yet: experimental\n");
 		break;
 	case B43_PHYTYPE_LP:
 		if (radio_id != 0x2062 && radio_id != 0x2063)
-- 
